UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 34, Lesson 4: Peer feedback', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nRewrite unkind \"This is boring\" into useful feedback on a legend ending.\n\nFEEDBACK\nUseful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\"\n\nCHECK\nVague praise alone does not help a writer improve.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nSwap stories with a peer or parent. Give two strengths and one improvement using the kind/specific/useful pattern. Write the feedback you received and one change you will make.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes.","lesson_number":4,"lesson_role":"Speaking and handwriting","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN2-OLC-01","EN2-HANDW-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Swap stories with a peer or parent. Give two strengths and one improvement using the kind/specific/useful pattern. Write the feedback you received and one change you will make. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original demonstration: \"Your place link was clear when you named the oval gum. Next, slow down on the storm sentence so we catch the threat.\" Kind + specific + useful.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve. Correction: Useful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\"\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve. Keep sample answers out of the child role.","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes.","Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event.","Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Understand and model\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.","Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding.","Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work.","Treat a missing detail as a stated fact."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Explain the evidence\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific error, then show how a revision fixes that error. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific error, then show how a revision fixes that error.","A superficial change in length or appearance does not repair meaning. Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve.","Treat a missing detail as a stated fact.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Test a misconception\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example. Review the result for accuracy and reader clarity. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example. Review the result for accuracy and reader clarity.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Transfer to an independent example\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Useful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\" Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["Useful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\"","Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Rewrite unkind \"This is boring\" into useful feedback on a legend ending.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["The most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Underline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Useful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\" Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["Useful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\"","A superficial change in length or appearance does not repair meaning. Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Describe why the warned-against approach would weaken your work, then write a co\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["The new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Make one fresh example demonstrating the skill and explain your main choice.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence, not repetition of the worked model, demonstrates the skill.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced relevant work with accurate reasoning and a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating the central skill, explaining the particular words or evidence that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original demonstration: \"Your place link was clear when you named the oval gum. Next, slow down on the storm sentence so we catch the threat.\" Kind + specific + useful.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A correction needs to change meaning or accuracy, not just make the text longer.","marking_guide":"Require an actual misconception plus corrected example and purpose-linked explanation.","question":"Name one likely error in using this skill, correct it and explain why the correction helps.","sample_answer":"Common error: Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve. Correction: Useful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\"","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent task and reflection, with explanations where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-eng-y3-w34-l4","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA alignment; verify content points before acceptance.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise peer feedback.","Read the mission before you start writing or speaking.","Keep the audience and purpose in mind as you work."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reason with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the evidence."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the wording that carries the meaning.","Then explain the choice without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore the example.","Prefer evidence over wording that merely sounds clever."],"submit":["Check that your response and reason are both present.","Proofread names, sequence and punctuation.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact word or action before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and underline one useful detail.","Say what that detail helps a reader understand.","A vague compliment is weaker than quoted evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with a stronger revision.","Change meaning or accuracy, not only length.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh topic that still uses the same skill.","Explain one decision in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include an original response and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new content."]},"subject":"English","success_criteria":["I can use peer feedback with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify kind and explain why it matters.","I can practise specific independently on a new prompt.","I can notice useful needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes. A supported explanation follows the actual words and purpose of the task.","options":["Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes.","A claim unrelated to the text.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no explanation."],"question":"What should you demonstrate in this teaching stage?"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\n\"Your place link was clear when you named the oval gum. Next, slow down on the storm sentence so we catch the threat.\" Kind + specific + useful.\n\nTRY FIRST\nRewrite unkind \"This is boring\" into useful feedback on a legend ending.\n\nFEEDBACK\nUseful: \"I lost the memory link at the end — can you name the place again in the last line?\"","explain":"Peer feedback should be kind, specific and useful — naming what worked and one clear improvement without unkind jokes.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Vague praise alone does not help a writer improve. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Feedback that is kind, specific and useful.","caption":"Name what worked and one improvement.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Kind + specific</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">place link clear: oval gum</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Useful next</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">slow on the storm sentence</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this 